Theorem (Legendre Symbol for Primes Greater Than 3):
Given a prime number \(p\) greater than 3, the Legendre symbol \(\left(\frac{3}{p}\right)\) equals 1 if \(p \mod 12\) is either 1 or 11, and -1 otherwise.
Formally, \(\left(\frac{3}{p}\right) = \begin{cases} 
  1 & \text{if } p \mod 12 \in \{1, 11\} \\
  -1 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}\)

